                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Sniper Ghost Warrior 3 has some enjoyable moments, particularly the long-range shooting mechanics. Adjusting your scope for distance, accounting for wind and bullet drop, and landing a clean headshot from several hundred metres away can be very satisfying.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, the rest of the game feels pretty average. The graphics are so-so, with unimpressive textures, repetitive environments, and character animations that feel dated.\r\n\r\nThe biggest disappointment is the open world. There's simply not much to do. Most missions follow the same formula: drive to a location, scout the area with your drone, tag enemies, find a good sniping position, eliminate targets, and move on. Clearing enemy outposts is fun initially, but after doing it several times, it becomes repetitive.\r\n\r\nEnemy AI doesn't help either. Sometimes enemies spot you from ridiculous distances, while other times they barely react when their buddies get shot nearby. Once you find a good elevated position, you can often clear an entire compound without much resistance.\r\n\r\nDriving around the map feels more like a chore than an adventure. There are occasional points of interest and collectibles, but very little meaningful activity between missions. Weapon customization is decent, although there's not enough variety in the gameplay to make experimenting with different loadouts particularly rewarding.\r\n\r\nOverall Sniper Ghost Warrior 3 isn't a bad game, but it feels like a missed opportunity. The sniping mechanics are solid, but the mediocre graphics, inconsistent AI, empty open world, and repetitive missions hold it back. Compared to Ghost Recon Wildlands, which offers much more tactical freedom, mission variety, and replayability, this game feels rather shallow.",
